{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"9b8cb87120388cb084ddbceed8094211f1cadd54f676c4f4253cfe88ddb8f47a","digest":{"component_or_area":"review-bot lifespan and reconciler","key_entities":["app.py:107","app.py:127-134","app.py:153","reconcile.py:215","reconcile.py:221","asyncio.Queue","asyncio.wait_for","SHUTDOWN_DRAIN_SECONDS","REVIEW_TIMEOUT_SECONDS","review_timeout_seconds()","docker-compose.yml","stop_grace_period"],"problem_keywords":["graceful shutdown","queue drain","review backlog","timeout resilience","autodeploy restart","reconciler hang","webhook loss"],"propositions":["On autodeploy restart, the review-bot's lifespan shutdown cancels the worker without draining the in-memory review queue, causing acknowledged-but-unreviewed webhook events to be silently lost until the reconciler backfill catches up.","The graceful shutdown must await queue.join() with a bounded timeout before canceling the worker, so queued events are processed and unprocessed items fall back to the reconciler.","The reconcile_once backfill function calls review_and_vote with no timeout, allowing a single hung review to freeze all reconciliation indefinitely.","The reconciler must wrap review_and_vote in asyncio.wait_for with the same timeout as the live worker, and continue to the next candidate on timeout rather than hang.","Docker's default stop_grace_period of 10s is insufficient for the drain window; stop_grace_period must be set to 60s on the review-bot service."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785821694947875451,"uuid":"8ab9f4a9-7613-45b9-9257-7edff89707f1"}